-a434-390b31123a28" :question/math-academy-id "q-123245" :question/problem "![](images/b3/b315be9ba524ab538388fdaad31161c280d7d6e5ab71261345063ac6ffe819d5.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](images/6c/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement $∇\\cdot F>0$ is true, whereas statements $∇\\cdot F=0$ and $∇\\cdot F<0$ are false. Notice that the lengths of the vectors increase as we move vertically and horizontally away from the origin. Therefore, the vector field $F$ acts like a source at every point.\n\n- Statement “$F$ is solenoidal” is false. Since $∇\\cdot F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $∇\\cdot F>0$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259554 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3260f191-357e-5fd6-b3f9-51c178134db5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257221} {:answer/id #uuid "6d128ce0-efb8-56e1-8023-f299f3be850c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257742} {:answer/id #uuid "b18c0515-7610-54e6-b101-c84deb16e608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258326} {:answer/id #uuid "f075feb5-f3f8-5129-a941-46db050b2214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258873} {:answer/id #uuid "f211cf5f-df49-5a9e-9bde-8f90da57b9b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b18c0515-7610-54e6-b101-c84deb16e608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258326} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b2b0b8a-76aa-5a6d-9974-c88122a91939" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259240}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3cac2494-d877-5849-8ad0-9d49fb79c7df" :question/math-academy-id "q-123753" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=1-{t}^{2},\\,\\,\\,y=3t+2,\\,-2\\le t\\le 2,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $a$ | $1$ | $0$ | $c$ |\n| $y$ | $-4$ | $-1$ | $b$ | $5$ | $8$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $x=1-{t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=1-(-1)^{2}=0.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $y=3t+2.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb=3(0)+2=2.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x=1-{t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n$$\nc=1-(2)^{2}=-3.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0+2+(-3)=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259555 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04f211ed-ddd7-5784-b0dc-35bcae2cefaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256825} {:answer/id #uuid "2de8af09-195f-5b8c-bab0-ef80dd63e84b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257188} {:answer/id #uuid "43228c86-2dad-5bf2-9955-abab71f85368" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257373} {:answer/id #uuid "7b84009a-c3a3-57ac-ba2b-c913c4990eb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257875} {:answer/id #uuid "8153caf4-964a-58e3-bef6-6c7992bf2466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04f211ed-ddd7-5784-b0dc-35bcae2cefaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256825} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d2fb483-072d-5aac-a385-71833c68e6fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259245}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "04aa985e-d3c5-5600-ac7a-83a47e2753a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-123755" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=4t,\\,\\,\\,y=-{t}^{3},\\,-3\\le t\\le 1,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-12$ | $-8$ | $a$ | $b$ | $4$ |\n| $y$ | $27$ | $8$ | $1$ | $0$ | $c$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $x=4t.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=4(-1)=-4.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $x=4t.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb=4(0)=0.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=1$ into $y=-{t}^{3}.$ This gives\n\n$$\nc=-(1)^{3}=-1.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-4+0+(-1)=-5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259556 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a77d04e-330f-5969-a265-1f92418525cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257159} {:answer/id #uuid "626a5119-9348-5540-b3a7-b85b3ca60c64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257650} {:answer/id #uuid "8a1a232f-2d58-5284-b6e0-3cf1d3a00e85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257995} {:answer/id #uuid "d5e8ee6a-3d7f-59d7-ace8-98f88ea43ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258658} {:answer/id #uuid "fd04b0fd-3ef4-5e4e-b82d-fabc59df44b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "626a5119-9348-5540-b3a7-b85b3ca60c64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257650} :answer-field/id #uuid "c11d5b8b-fe59-57a7-8e6b-14dd5adaef71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2de12943-54f8-500d-9e95-bde9a205cbca" :question/math-academy-id "q-123763" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2\\sqrt{t+9},\\,\\,\\,y=t+1,\\,t\\ge 0,\n$$\n\nwhat is the range of $x?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the range of $x,$ note that $\\sqrt{t+9}\\ge 3$ for all $t\\ge 0.$ Consequently, $x=2\\sqrt{t+9}\\ge 6.$\n\nTherefore, we can conclude that $x\\ge 6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259557 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fc92ce1-7d99-535d-8470-6bc513682293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le -4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257039} {:answer/id #uuid "2a2e93ef-86d7-5dbc-848f-aca59b976bdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257154} {:answer/id #uuid "7eda883f-3d24-5b1c-b928-523fd6537cd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257912} {:answer/id #uuid "8dcfa983-5ef3-5c2e-9c9a-f6886ae38ec3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258029} {:answer/id #uuid "de9f47c6-7fdd-57a8-bdac-638af6b59ada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7eda883f-3d24-5b1c-b928-523fd6537cd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257912} :answer-field/id #uuid "01f4ba3a-bccf-5208-8e4a-9fe56858b468" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259034}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "808ba9b8-7fbd-5187-9780-5105c365918f" :question/math-academy-id "q-123764" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=3t-7,\\,\\,\\,y=1-t,\\,t\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nwhat is the range of $x?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the range of $x,$ note that $x=3t-7\\ge -4$ for all $t\\ge 1.$ \n\nConsequently, the range of $x$ is $x\\ge -4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 175